# AI Usage Log - Sprint 1

--> Task 1.1: User Profile Template
Purpose of AI Use: Generate a template for the user profile
Chat Link or Prompt/Response: https://chatgpt.com/c/6ab9a338-9bd8-83ea-9a6c-bf944929fd7e
AI-Suggested Content: AI provided a generated image of the template.
Validation: Analyzed it to see if it matched the requirements of the sprint and what was agreed amongst team members.
Decision: Decided to place the user profile and the Edit Profile section on separate pages because I thought it would look tight on one page.
Reflection: AI gave me inspiration on how the user page could look. Since it produced an image, not code, I still had to interpret the design and decide how to structure the pages myself.
Responsible person: Ariane

--> Task 1.2: CareerConnect Logo
Purpose of AI Use: Generate a .png CareerConnect logo named "CareerConnect" with blue and white theme for a Job Search and Application Tracking Platform with transparent background and not tag line underneath. (Claude AI was used).
Chat Link or Prompt/Response: Generated logo used in the project
AI-Suggested Content: Provided a logo that matched the prompt. 
Validation: Made sure the team approved of the logo.
Decision: Used the logo as it was.
Reflection: AI helped me generate a unique logo which we would use for the entire project.
Responsible person: Ariane

--> Task 1.3: Navigation bar and header
Purpose of AI Use: Used Copilot in VS Code to generate blue and white themed code to style the navigation bar and header, using the template generated by ChatGPT in Task 1.1.
Chat Link or Prompt/Response: The original Copilot chat is not available (the session history could not be recovered). The prompt, as best I remember, was to generate the CSS for the project's files based on the uploaded design image. The exact wording cannot be confirmed.
AI-Suggested Content: It generated a blue-and-white themed CSS stylesheet to style the navigation bar and header: blue fixed header, white vertical sidebar, white hamburger toggle.
Validation: Applied the suggested code and opened the page in the browser to see if the changes made sense.
Decision: Accepted all CSS code for the navigation bar. For the styling of the header, the size of the logo was made smaller and all other changes were accepted.
Reflection: AI saved time on the repetitive styling and gave a consistent blue and white theme. It is a good starting point, but I still need to review its output.
Responsible person: Ariane

--> Task 1.4: User Information page styling
Purpose of AI Use: Used Copilot in VS Code to generate blue and white themed code to style the User Information page, using the template generated by ChatGPT in Task 1.1.
Chat Link or Prompt/Response: The original Copilot chat is not available (the session history could not be recovered). The prompt, as best I remember, was to generate the CSS for the project's files based on the uploaded design image. The exact wording cannot be confirmed.
AI-Suggested Content: It generated a blue-and-white themed CSS stylesheet to style the User Information page: presentable profile-summary card with blue edit button, defined profile picture shape, and blue and white themed camera button at the edge of the profile picture.
Validation: Applied the suggested code and opened the page in the browser to see if the changes made sense.
Decision: Fixed a card box for the profile picture and information, centralized the name and status (Jobseeker and Employer), and placed all other information to the left on the profile card. Accepted all other changes. The skills information and its design were added later by my teammate, Aminata.
Reflection: AI is fast at producing a first version, but I had to check it to make sure the design was well proportioned and matched what I wanted.
Responsible person: Ariane

--> Task 1.5: Edit profile page styling
Purpose of AI Use: Used Copilot in VS Code to generate blue and white themed code to style the Edit Profile page, using the template generated by ChatGPT in Task 1.1.
Chat Link or Prompt/Response: The original Copilot chat is not available (the session history could not be recovered). The prompt, as best I remember, was to generate the CSS for the project's files based on the uploaded design image. The exact wording cannot be confirmed.
AI-Suggested Content: It generated a blue-and-white themed CSS stylesheet to style the Edit Profile page: responsive two-column edit form, styled Save/Cancel buttons.
Validation: Applied the suggested code and opened the page in the browser to see if the changes made sense.
Decision: Accepted and used all CSS code suggestions.
Reflection: AI worked well for a standard form layout like this one. Since the design image was clear, the generated CSS worked without changes.
Responsible person: Ariane
